WEBVTT

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:47.210
Your Majesty, I'm sorry to disturb you, but I would like to remind you once again that according to the researchers, your plan is a Russian roulette.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:57.680
Our knowledge of phenomena like the Matorer is at best theoretical, but it is probably the continuous worsening of the disturbances caused by it.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.000
Well, that was new.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.400
Can you drive through it?

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:07.670
The numerical torque pressure in the engine is several teraparsecs.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.670
Our ships are not designed for these conditions.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:11.670
So you don't have a brain?

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.150
You fool.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:20.480
People can't resist the Nath all the time.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.670
I'd try to be in my position sometimes.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.670
It's not that easy when you have to decide all the things in the world yourself.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:37.970
I think that Moppo would have lost his hand even worse.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:41.840
This whole mess started 8 years ago when my ship was destroyed.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:47.520
And I got stuck in the past with the stupid robot and the smelly Plingon psychopath.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:51.400
We destroyed our own roads and dissolved the local population.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.900
So that history was just a distraction.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.270
The life of a normal person was not very pleasant.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.000
The only good thing was the Purilaises.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.050
with double shaders.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:38.660
Hi.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.040
By the way, I'm Captain Pirk.

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:56.890
Aha.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.000
I'm from the future.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:06.530
Hey, I've got a cold too.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.960
Hey, please. That's a clear super-sucker.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.690
No, it's not.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.950
Your hand is stuck here, stupid.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.310
Alright.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:18.650
Hey, I'll call Info.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.000
I've got a communicator here.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.220
It can prove that I'm really who I am.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:25.760
Yeah, no need to bother.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.240
Fuck you, you don't have to eat that!

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.440
What the fuck is wrong with you?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.440
You better stop or I'll shoot you!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.440
That's a fucking super sofa!

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.260
Damn it, I got my hands on it!

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:48.260
It's starting to hurt, dammit!

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:51.170
It could be that you're about to get hurt.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.140
My batteries are running out!

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.920
No! I can't breathe!

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.690
No! No! No!

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:16.890
This is a nice surprise. You haven't heard of it, have you?

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:20.890
Well, info doesn't always have time to disturb the timeline.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:24.290
I think this momentary silence will be enough.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:29.090
Same words. The old country isn't really as barbaric as it seems.

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:33.470
This place is really boring.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.640
Excuse me sir.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.940
Three saunas and one meat pie.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:39.060
We'll eat here.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.560
Wait a minute.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.330
Excuse me sir.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:50.550
I can't take this for a minute.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:56.170
Don't you dare barge into my yard!

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:59.160
This place is closed!

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:07.080
Listen, I've been waiting. We don't need to meet up and plan for the future.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:12.420
Call me and we'll meet up at our base tomorrow.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:18.790
Got it. I'll call you immediately when I get rid of these ghosts. I'll be coming through the windows soon.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:25.410
Damn you yellow-haired scum! I'll take you to the yard and I'll make a mess out of you!

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:41.780
The arrival of the Bulgarians was supposed to be the beginning of a new generation of the human race.

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:49.680
The top-notch people arrived to the planet almost by accident and then decided to join the band of the rock star Jeff Cockbrain.

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:54.600
It was a mistake to leave it in the hands of a drunkard.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:59.120
After that, the Bulgarians didn't even dare to cross the border with the human race.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:12.920
Fortunately, I had a backup plan to save the situation.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:19.780
That's where Info and Dwarf got the permission to help.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:22.900
Captain, I hope you have a good reason to call us to your base.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.780
This meeting can speed up the timeline from the past.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.140
In fact, it is.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:30.000
You're right.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:30.500
This.

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:34.230
Wives lesbo-ing their husbands by promise.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.530
No, I mean...

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.240
This.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:46.000
This is a surprising twist.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.390
The entire international space project has been shut down.

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:52.790
We shouldn't have gone like that in our history book.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:53.840
No.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:58.960
Just today, the Kennedy Space Center had to announce a breakthrough in the antimatter reactor.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:08:59.960
So that's why we have to do it.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:01.940
to take action on their own.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:03.690
They are founded by their own P-Union.

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:06.540
Unconditional action is against the first directive.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:10.740
But if we don't do it, the timeline will be ruined anyway!

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:13.100
Well, how else can we get peace to the people,

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.820
a united language,

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.720
long-lasting tricone-uniforms

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:20.000
and an army that defends the high?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.220
If I am always the captain of the P-Union, I decide

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:26.260
that we will ensure the birth of the P-Union in any way possible!

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:30.000
Hmm... Technology of the future in the minds of today's people could lead to

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.000
That's why the world needs a power leader.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.000
Like others.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:40.010
I'm going to be a emperor.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:43.010
One heavy crusader should be enough to rule this country.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:45.270
Everyone would be valued.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:48.050
Unfortunately, we don't have a crusader.

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:51.050
And we can't build one without an anti-material reactor,

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:53.910
which is impossible to build with modern technology.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:56.960
But I know where we can get such a reactor.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:59.280
Give me the phone.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.330
Cockbrain? -Pirt here.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:09.470
Oh, hello. -Where's the ship?

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:11.920
Ship? Oh, the Bulgarian rocket.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.920
We sold it to a Russian guy.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.920
He said it was damn good.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.870
For whom?

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.850
Vladimir or something.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:22.160
I don't remember. -Where does Vladimir live?

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.020
At the nuclear power plant.

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.020
Or something like that.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:30.000
Who the hell gave you the permission to sell the ship?

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:33.560
- Me too. - Same goes for you, Satan.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:48.520
- Satan the coward has sold his ship to Russia! - Goddamnit!

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:54.410
- What the hell are we going to do now? - Well, of course we're going to Russia.

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:59.860
Fortunately, the missing Vulgar rocket was found surprisingly easily by the Russian research institute.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:06.940
It was actually the only place in the whole planet where I could find the necessary parts of my new flagship.

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:28.440
Arsene, Arsene!

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:29.440
What is it?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.500
WHERE?

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.280
I RETURN TO TECHNOLOGY!

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:35.800
Vladimir!

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.690
The reactor has overheated!

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:40.180
The cooling system is somewhat weak!

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:41.630
Goddammit!

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.330
And the whole control system is stuck again!

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:45.850
Sergei!

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:46.850
Sergei!

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:49.250
Where is that Sergei Luha?

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:50.940
What?

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.260
You served in the previous nuclear power plant.

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:55.260
Yeah, in Chernobyl.

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:56.260
What now?

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.260
The reactor has no cooling.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.000
But you know these things.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:03.270
Get the reactor truck and find out who's the last one!

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:05.190
Yes, thank you!

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:11.130
Chernobyl. Why does that name sound familiar?

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:14.140
Chernobyl?

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:17.070
Chernobyl!

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:17.990
Fire!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:33.590
-Rokefair! -Rokefair!

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:59.700
-You're not a hero, you're a villain! -No!

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:05.630
Yes, Mr. Captain. I thought it was the ventilation in my room.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:08.240
It was cold.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:25.220
Jacob, Jacob. Someday I'll take you prisoner and you do as I say and it starts to rain.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:30.000
Is this some kind of coup d'etat?

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.890
Yeah, you could say that.

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:37.200
Finally! A new Soviet Union is born!

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:41.340
Our people are divided under the banner of capitalism!

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:43.450
Hooray!

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:47.670
What the hell? Don't they want to fight?

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:52.970
You should play along.

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:54.920
Yes, I am Emperor Pirkia.

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:57.150
We are building a new army here in Tatsania,

00:13:57.150 --> 00:14:00.000
which will start a new great empire.

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.460
That's how it started.

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:10.930
From the village of Sanistan, surrounded by the research institute,

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:14.910
there was enough space and workforce to establish the P-liit.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:18.710
Info managed to lead the construction work of our new flagship,

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:20.670
while I had better things to do.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:26.640
I gave clear instructions that the ship had to be ready in six months.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:30.000
But the tuners succeeded in destroying my expensive ship for years.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.620
I don't want to waste any of my time.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:35.570
I used the money for good, though.

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:37.570
The leader has to be a charismatic character.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:39.570
So I got the food.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:43.720
The training was tough.

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:45.620
But I managed to survive.

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:47.800
Right away.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.690
Electro Force, what do I do?

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:53.110
Only 5999 rubles.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.370
You fucking bastard.

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:44.240
At the same time, the negotiations with the Russian president about the common future had gone well.

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:49.680
Without a strong ally, nothing would have come out of my plans.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:21.210
Take a look at this.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.290
Isn't it fun to meet people?

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:30.000
Yeah, we have this contract we were talking about.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:39.400
Krasnaya, Ljubljana, Ljubljana, let's look through this document.

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:44.040
It's good, just like we all agreed.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.460
I can't look through it.

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:56.500
We used to write, "Igor Kynia, we will make this world a better place."

00:16:56.500 --> 00:17:00.000
Union with Russia.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.000
and started a wide array of military equipment.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.500
The equipment started to be in good condition

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.800
and the training of the troops went well according to the plans.

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:21.100
Don't take anything from me!

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:24.350
A moment that I had been waiting for the most,

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:26.240
came to an end.

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:30.000
Our army began to be in good shape and it was finally time to reveal

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:55.140
We'll give the world our national flag, the flag of the B-Union, C.P.P. Potkustart.

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:56.680
Looks like it.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:18:00.000
Hmph! Tactics is still missing a chair!

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.000
and he would want your massive travel flesh to crumble.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:14.410
Are we ready to go?

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:15.400
Yes, sir.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:19.750
Power level 96.3%.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:22.390
Aren't we going to conquer the world?

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:27.630
Or was there something else to ask?

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:30.000
I mean, are you the one who has the power?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.300
I've talked a lot about you, Emperor Pirk.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:41.080
Yeah, here I am in all my glory.

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:48.440
Right.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:49.970
Let's get going.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.570
I don't have any skills left in Moscow anymore.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:25.380
Welcome to C.P.P. Potkustart.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:29.830
Mr. President, I'm sure you're interested to see what my ship is capable of.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:34.070
There is a great power.

00:20:34.070 --> 00:20:37.470
First we will show the people our new weapon.

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:47.070
The full rotation! Now!

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:55.070
It will cost again!

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:57.370
It will make a huge Russian army!

00:20:57.370 --> 00:21:00.000
What? Russian quality?

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:06.360
Due to the impurities of the antimatter gas, the power of the engines is enough only to reach the rotation times of two.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:10.480
Worf, take that chopper target, let's see if it even works.

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:12.990
No, no.

00:21:12.990 --> 00:21:15.150
It's a gold light bulb and a light bulb.

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:28.490
It wasn't just American, but we spent billions of rubles on it.

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:30.000
Stop it now, Pappo.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:37.530
Let's make this place a better place!

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:42.090
The propaganda agency of the B-Union presents:

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:47.140
"The goal of victory"

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:52.770
The third millennium opened a world where unemployment, hunger and diseases

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:55.890
ravaged the people without mercy.

00:21:55.890 --> 00:22:00.000
The leaders of the great powers spoke of freedom, but they were torn apart

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:05.410
from his mother's shoulders to fight in a meaningless war.

00:22:05.410 --> 00:22:09.950
But from the barbed wire rose a hero who found his place,

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:13.200
the mother of Russia from a strong stake.

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:18.590
As the waves rushed, Emperor Pirk and President Uljanov

00:22:18.590 --> 00:22:24.410
stood on the edge of our light road towards a new world order.

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:30.000
The journey was long, but we did not get tired and proved that nothing

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:31.790
was not impossible.

00:22:31.790 --> 00:22:36.800
Our people were ready for the last battle of mankind.

00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:41.300
The heroes of the motherland led our great army

00:22:41.300 --> 00:22:45.480
to liberate our northern brotherly nation from the night of Sorra.

00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:50.080
Together, the noble men of Russia and the technology of the future

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:52.680
formed an invincible front

00:22:52.680 --> 00:22:57.210
in front of which the old world would be victorious.

00:22:57.210 --> 00:22:59.920
In front of the majesty of Emperor Pirk,

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:06.920
The enemy was powerless and the hands of rebellion were pushed aside from the new human road.

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:16.550
In the face of a certain defeat, the rulers fled and the winds of freedom blew in the empty cities.

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:23.920
However, Europe did not offer a safe place for the rebels.

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:30.000
As a victory, our army marched forward towards a better world

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.840
"The roaring of the saapaids roared over the seas and mountains..."

00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:37.430
"...stabbing our enemies' land like the Ukkos."

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:43.860
"Soon our troops struck their target in the heart of the old Mantere."

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:51.700
"When Europe was free, the eyes of the nations turned toward the great Satan of the old world..."

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:54.140
"...the United States of America."

00:23:54.140 --> 00:24:00.000
"Unwillingly, they floated the skies to death, which was their fate."

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.920
to their own destination.

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:05.600
The time of the old beast had come.

00:24:05.600 --> 00:24:09.710
With the help of iron and manpower we taught them

00:24:09.710 --> 00:24:13.880
what real freedom meant.

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:17.880
The time was finally ripe for a new, brilliant empire.

00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:20.930
The P-Union was born.

00:24:31.210 --> 00:24:35.670
That's it.

00:24:35.670 --> 00:24:41.160
What? What did you hold on to?

00:24:41.160 --> 00:24:44.150
I'm your president! Get rid of him!

00:24:44.150 --> 00:24:49.130
You! You too! You're a cheater!

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:52.100
You're a tyrant! We have an agreement!

00:24:52.100 --> 00:24:55.110
You're Per Savitz! No, don't shoot me!

00:24:55.110 --> 00:24:59.110
Don't shoot me! No, don't shoot me!

00:25:10.520 --> 00:25:15.630
The world's only sovereign came to me, the Emperor.

00:25:15.630 --> 00:25:23.810
All the resorts of the united people were directed to the construction of the war ships of the P-Union.

00:25:23.810 --> 00:25:29.800
They had to be ships, so that the veiled faces of the whole world wouldn't be able to jump into their eyes.

00:25:30.800 --> 00:25:35.000
Even though I did everything for humanity, I still can't thank them enough.

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:38.830
The people just had to choose from countless small problems.

00:25:38.830 --> 00:25:42.640
Such as overpopulation, hunger and other uselessness.

00:26:07.320 --> 00:26:12.310
I thought then that the problems could be solved by expanding the B-unit to other planets.

00:26:12.310 --> 00:26:18.240
Well, our ships were just so primitive that we couldn't get very far with them.

00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:21.170
There were no inhabited planets nearby.

00:26:21.170 --> 00:26:25.200
We did try a few, but the results were a bit lame.

00:26:39.120 --> 00:26:43.030
The CPP Kalinka was a cheap-to-do company,

00:26:43.030 --> 00:26:47.200
whose task was to patrol the more backward sectors for a couple of years,

00:26:47.200 --> 00:26:49.090
or until it rots away.

00:26:49.090 --> 00:26:52.920
The captain had, of course, chosen a task to keep an eye on.

00:27:07.870 --> 00:27:13.870
Sergei Foucault to CPP Kalinka's unrecognized ship, report!

00:27:13.870 --> 00:27:17.700
Sir, Emperor Pirck's third directive.

00:27:17.700 --> 00:27:22.500
All incoming AIP fleet ships are to be destroyed immediately.

00:27:30.190 --> 00:27:34.980
Weird. I checked the ship just before the explosion.

00:27:34.980 --> 00:27:40.220
There was only one living thing inside. A human.

00:27:40.220 --> 00:27:44.250
But how can a single person's ship be this far from Earth?

00:27:44.250 --> 00:27:48.820
I don't know. Let's call the Emperor.

00:27:48.820 --> 00:27:56.580
What?

00:27:56.580 --> 00:27:59.000
We tested the ship in the Epsilon Quadrant.

00:27:59.000 --> 00:27:59.510
What?

00:28:00.250 --> 00:28:02.720
It was a human's ability, but we destroyed it.

00:28:02.720 --> 00:28:06.280
Have you gone to hell to save your own life?

00:28:06.280 --> 00:28:09.250
You have the right to war.

00:28:09.250 --> 00:28:11.370
Who the hell paid you?

00:28:11.370 --> 00:28:14.450
You did, but it wasn't the P-League team.

00:28:14.450 --> 00:28:17.530
That's what I'm talking about, I'm blind.

00:28:17.530 --> 00:28:21.470
I can't even see from here.

00:28:21.470 --> 00:28:25.030
Who did this to Jalle?

00:28:52.430 --> 00:28:53.490
Well, what?

00:28:53.490 --> 00:28:55.730
We had agreed to meet at two o'clock.

00:28:55.730 --> 00:29:00.000
Don't you fucking wise men think that it's two o'clock in the afternoon?

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:04.150
that you are clearly eating yourself.

00:29:04.150 --> 00:29:08.300
In any case, my case concerns Captain Fakov's report.

00:29:08.300 --> 00:29:11.010
What about it?

00:29:11.010 --> 00:29:14.100
I analyzed the possible routes of their encounter with the ship.

00:29:14.100 --> 00:29:17.690
And considering the shape of the ship, the only possible conclusion is

00:29:17.690 --> 00:29:20.450
that the ship's origin is close to the other side of the Matryoshka.

00:29:20.450 --> 00:29:22.530
Yeah, yeah. Let's get to the point.

00:29:22.530 --> 00:29:24.330
Since the ship didn't belong to the B-Flight,

00:29:24.330 --> 00:29:29.190
we can conclude that behind the Matryoshka is another unknown human civilization.

00:29:29.190 --> 00:29:30.000
Taking into account

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:32.950
This is probably the most difficult situation... - We can destroy their planets!

00:29:32.950 --> 00:29:37.590
I was going to suggest asking for help. - Yeah, but you don't get it.

00:29:37.590 --> 00:29:40.440
Is the battle in the ship ready?

00:30:04.060 --> 00:30:09.100
Good bloody captains. You have been summoned here for one reason.

00:30:09.100 --> 00:30:16.560
We have a reason to believe that behind this material there is a nice place to live.

00:30:16.560 --> 00:30:19.950
And we will take it with us if it is necessary.

00:30:19.950 --> 00:30:24.810
You have been given a piece of paper from which you can see your mission.

00:30:24.810 --> 00:30:26.730
I don't have any papers.

00:30:26.730 --> 00:30:29.850
Fuck off. If you ever interfere again, I will send you to hell.

00:30:30.060 --> 00:30:31.960
Bring the rest of the floor!

00:30:31.960 --> 00:30:35.030
You sit on top of them.

00:30:37.040 --> 00:30:40.440
We use all the equipment available for this mission.

00:30:40.440 --> 00:30:41.440
Oh yeah.

00:30:41.440 --> 00:30:43.440
There is no way to fail.

00:30:43.440 --> 00:30:47.180
That's why I'm going to lead this mission personally.

00:30:47.180 --> 00:30:49.680
And then you can get out of it.

00:30:49.680 --> 00:30:51.410
Departure tomorrow at six o'clock.

00:30:51.410 --> 00:30:53.240
Do you have anything to ask?

00:30:53.240 --> 00:30:56.180
Hello.

00:32:16.960 --> 00:32:27.170
Turlehtilas plus. Welcome to Babel 13. We've been waiting for you for weeks.

00:32:31.470 --> 00:32:32.350
May I ask a question?

00:32:32.350 --> 00:32:33.630
Yes.

00:32:33.630 --> 00:32:40.590
Nothing.

00:32:40.590 --> 00:32:44.550
Okay, excuse me Eric.

00:32:44.550 --> 00:32:47.690
There's been some news in the room.

00:32:47.690 --> 00:32:56.700
This is the security chief of the station, Mihail Karikrandi.

00:32:56.700 --> 00:32:58.200
A bit of a shrewd attitude.

00:32:58.200 --> 00:32:59.370
This is important to me.

00:32:59.370 --> 00:33:00.000
What the fuck are you talking about?

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:14.640
What are you talking about? Lieutenant Kehveli had lying in his bed last night in the starflurry and had gone for a walk.

00:33:14.640 --> 00:33:16.840
What? Why didn't you stop him?

00:33:16.840 --> 00:33:22.410
Well, since I was there, I went to sleep at that time.

00:33:22.410 --> 00:33:25.880
Well, where is Kehveli now?

00:33:25.880 --> 00:33:29.800
Well, there he is. He hadn't come in the morning, so I sent a search party after him.

00:33:30.760 --> 00:33:36.330
They haven't found anything else but this.

00:33:36.330 --> 00:33:49.000
Oh my god, the Mucalans have turned the Gevel into a salt mine.

00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:52.120
Yeah, this is a datacrystal.

00:33:52.120 --> 00:33:55.600
It was used to store Gevel's ship, you know.

00:34:01.210 --> 00:34:18.460
Salt as a spice.

00:34:18.460 --> 00:34:27.680
What kind of a firecracker was that?

00:34:27.680 --> 00:34:30.000
I don't know.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.790
At least that's what I think.

00:34:31.790 --> 00:34:33.390
Could this mean?

00:34:33.390 --> 00:34:34.360
What?

00:34:34.360 --> 00:34:37.300
The predictions of the minibar are true.

00:34:37.300 --> 00:34:43.340
The great darkness is coming, and we're all going to die.

00:34:43.340 --> 00:34:49.000
Now take it seriously, Joni.

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:51.000
The one who destroys, devours and destroys the darkness.

00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:56.800
I've read his book too, but let's go back to reality, Jouko.

00:34:56.800 --> 00:34:57.980
Good night.

00:35:03.320 --> 00:35:10.120
There you have it, Mihail. We have to trust our feats, as they guided our ancestors thousands of years ago.

00:35:10.120 --> 00:35:20.820
Ivanoitza, we need helpers. Ask the globe to send all the ships of the nearby sector to us.

00:35:20.820 --> 00:35:25.360
Yes, sir.

00:35:25.360 --> 00:35:26.690
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:35:46.920 --> 00:35:48.200
Here's what happened.

00:35:48.460 --> 00:35:49.900
Let's put it this way.

00:35:51.020 --> 00:35:52.520
Fako, you go first.

00:35:53.080 --> 00:35:56.960
Emperor, we don't know if the star ship will make it through that material.

00:35:56.960 --> 00:35:58.880
That's why Fako goes first.

00:35:59.240 --> 00:36:00.000
Oh yeah!

00:36:31.690 --> 00:36:32.500
Not better.

00:37:00.320 --> 00:37:03.940
Info. Compression. SOMETHING!

00:37:03.940 --> 00:37:07.420
I'm compressing the Hindenburg resistance to the ion field.

00:37:07.420 --> 00:37:12.940
Quartoni crystals should have the correct reaction frequency reading just now.

00:37:12.940 --> 00:37:19.000
Yeah, how so?

00:37:19.000 --> 00:37:22.000
Sir. Unidentified ships visible.

00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:22.850
Telkkari.

00:37:31.210 --> 00:37:37.280
They disappeared. At least there aren't any planets in the Monster Hill.

00:37:37.280 --> 00:37:41.560
The ships are apparently activating some kind of local orbit in the open.

00:37:41.560 --> 00:37:45.920
We can track their energy discharge, which should open another opposite orbit.

00:37:45.920 --> 00:37:49.080
Well, if you just made it so I could explain.

00:37:49.080 --> 00:37:50.900
Ruori, let's follow them.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:38.070
The main reinforcements. Now we can open the jump gate.

00:38:38.070 --> 00:38:39.070
We'll get through the ships.

00:38:39.070 --> 00:38:40.240
How many?

00:38:40.240 --> 00:38:43.190
Forty. A guy. Unknown.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:05.790
I didn't even know this when I received the command of the station.

00:39:05.790 --> 00:39:10.660
Of course I would have received it with a greater enthusiasm than ever before.

00:39:10.660 --> 00:39:13.480
The purpose of this station is to protect peace.

00:39:13.480 --> 00:39:17.560
And even though we would have to kill every intelligent being in this galaxy, peace-

00:39:17.560 --> 00:39:20.620
Captain! This suspicion is the right time to speak.

00:39:20.620 --> 00:39:23.190
This is a matter of principle.

00:39:23.190 --> 00:39:30.000
My right is to speak, and I swear by rock and stone that no one, no one,

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:41.360
You don't have that right from me. Not the enemy fleet, not even a broken commander whose career is to be the captain of a trash can that tries to steal the invasions!

00:39:41.360 --> 00:39:46.130
Is that clear?

00:40:08.250 --> 00:40:11.150
Sir, we are being called.

00:40:11.150 --> 00:40:18.650
Well, put on your helmet.

00:40:23.520 --> 00:40:26.310
This is Captain Sherrypie, Babel 13.

00:40:26.310 --> 00:40:30.000
Please inform us.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:32.020
They're just humans.

00:40:32.020 --> 00:40:35.390
This is Emperor Pirk, the leader of Peliton.

00:40:35.390 --> 00:40:39.500
Info. That's some space station.

00:40:39.500 --> 00:40:41.500
What about that planet? Is it a residential area?

00:40:41.500 --> 00:40:43.430
According to the geologists, no, sir.

00:40:43.430 --> 00:40:45.100
Of course.

00:40:45.100 --> 00:40:48.920
We just came to say hello, when we were walking around nearby.

00:40:48.920 --> 00:40:51.060
At this airport.

00:40:51.060 --> 00:40:52.870
By the way, where are you at home?

00:40:52.870 --> 00:40:55.830
Uh... This station is a defenseless area.

00:40:55.830 --> 00:40:59.670
We have visitors from Minibar, Kentucky, Narsk...

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:02.400
Of course from the peripheries and the Earth.

00:41:02.400 --> 00:41:06.550
What? We haven't been here before.

00:41:06.550 --> 00:41:11.050
Emperor, let's assume we've come to our own world, a mirror to the universe.

00:41:11.050 --> 00:41:14.850
History here has led to different developments, but some of the elements are familiar.

00:41:14.850 --> 00:41:16.930
Do you know where their planet is?

00:41:16.930 --> 00:41:22.180
In theory, yes. It is assumed that the relative locations of the stars are the same as our computer knows.

00:41:22.180 --> 00:41:26.710
Another planet?

00:41:26.710 --> 00:41:29.160
Well, we'll conquer that.

00:41:29.160 --> 00:41:30.000
Let's make sure that the material

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:34.460
"The head of the murderer, the suspicion is the destruction of Pötkölä, where it takes a long time to..."

00:41:34.460 --> 00:41:34.960
"There..."

00:41:34.960 --> 00:41:37.260
"Kaiser! The contact is still open!"

00:41:37.260 --> 00:41:40.400
"I know that!"

00:41:40.400 --> 00:41:42.130
*cough*

00:41:42.130 --> 00:41:50.960
"That day, when I joined the army, my father said to me:"

00:41:50.960 --> 00:41:59.540
"My son, you have not been blessed with great gifts of wisdom, nor can you enrich your mother with that face."

00:42:00.320 --> 00:42:04.460
But you are a human.

00:42:04.460 --> 00:42:09.640
You came from Earth, and you are coming back to Earth.

00:42:09.640 --> 00:42:14.640
So show your father's potential and get out of that bed!

00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:19.010
So I don't have to lose my eyes!

00:42:19.010 --> 00:42:21.600
Situation. Can we beat them?

00:42:21.600 --> 00:42:25.720
Taking into account that we have Kimmott's gear and they don't, we have a possibility.

00:42:25.720 --> 00:42:26.720
Yes or no?

00:42:26.720 --> 00:42:30.000
Yes.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:32.000
I need you today.

00:42:32.000 --> 00:42:35.140
Stop the lightbulb and send a message to the rest of the fleet.

00:42:35.140 --> 00:42:37.140
I'll see Kömbe out of the bed.

00:42:37.140 --> 00:42:41.130
And I gave the doctor to take his blood sample.

00:42:41.130 --> 00:42:43.550
Piru, take it.

00:42:43.550 --> 00:42:45.550
The Earth needs me again today.

00:42:45.550 --> 00:42:47.550
Open fire at the lightbulb at the maximum range.

00:42:47.550 --> 00:42:50.550
Get the fleet to paint the pictures and wait for my mark.

00:42:50.550 --> 00:43:00.000
I'm sure that every man, every woman and every child in this station knows Saara.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:07.080
You will rule the world only over our dead bodies!

00:43:07.080 --> 00:43:15.540
Know that you can pay a high price for every deciliter of our space.

00:43:15.540 --> 00:43:20.710
We attack a rock or a pebble.

00:43:20.710 --> 00:43:24.920
And if the pebbles fall, we attack a rock with our bare hands!

00:43:24.920 --> 00:43:28.380
The limit of darkness is taken by this!

00:43:28.380 --> 00:43:30.000
And even if it takes you to hell,

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.300
...for a thousand years.

00:43:32.300 --> 00:43:34.300
Eat balls of light.

00:43:34.300 --> 00:43:36.300
Fire.

00:44:05.760 --> 00:44:09.450
The enemy is in front of us!

00:44:09.450 --> 00:44:11.310
Shut down the break-ins!

00:44:11.310 --> 00:44:15.920
Activate the defense network!

00:44:15.920 --> 00:44:18.600
Good talk.

00:44:37.930 --> 00:44:42.400
I hereby declare that the Amiga-class destroyers have reached optimal firing distance.

00:44:42.400 --> 00:44:49.120
Order them to concentrate on the heavier ships.

00:44:49.120 --> 00:44:53.400
The first shot has to show that we are real.

00:44:53.400 --> 00:44:58.800
Fire!

00:45:21.980 --> 00:45:30.000
- I'm not going to! - That's disgusting! It seems like the nature doesn't like this size.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:44.340
I don't even know how to register this energy.

00:45:44.340 --> 00:45:46.230
We've got a long way to go.

00:45:46.230 --> 00:45:48.220
The gas is spilling everywhere.

00:45:48.220 --> 00:45:50.160
And the coffee chain is broken.

00:45:50.160 --> 00:45:52.170
We can't get to Toivonrikka in any way.

00:45:52.170 --> 00:45:54.170
It's a bit of a drag, so we'll make it to the island.

00:45:54.170 --> 00:45:56.170
But I don't need two hours.

00:45:56.170 --> 00:46:00.000
Two minutes?!

00:46:00.250 --> 00:46:29.800
I just noticed that we only have three light bulbs left in our storage.

00:46:30.670 --> 00:46:33.270
I'll make an official selection of my ship's sub-equipment.

00:46:33.270 --> 00:46:34.430
Stop it, Narina!

00:46:34.430 --> 00:46:36.440
A woman is good at using tweezers.

00:47:13.080 --> 00:47:20.040
Rackkama is facing an overwhelming opponent, and I can't stand this any longer.

00:47:33.260 --> 00:47:36.500
Damn. Looks good.

00:47:36.500 --> 00:47:42.180
I'm afraid we only have one more option left.

00:47:42.180 --> 00:47:43.100
You mean...

00:47:43.100 --> 00:47:50.280
Yes. We have time to play.

00:47:50.280 --> 00:47:57.110
I'll keep my word. Open up to the enemy command ship.

00:48:03.360 --> 00:48:05.670
Wait a minute. We're being called from the station.

00:48:05.670 --> 00:48:16.620
Saanen notices that if Sherrypie doesn't give his life for the sake of the best propaganda material...

00:48:16.620 --> 00:48:21.700
Just put it if it's that important to you.

00:48:21.700 --> 00:48:30.000
Babel 13 is giving up. Don't shoot.

00:48:30.640 --> 00:48:32.640
There are more than a quarter million civilians here.

00:48:32.640 --> 00:48:34.550
I'm interested in your civilians.

00:48:34.550 --> 00:48:38.010
They're everywhere.

00:48:38.010 --> 00:48:40.830
What the fuck am I doing in a full-blown army base?

00:48:40.830 --> 00:48:44.130
You could bring your men to a vacation for a while.

00:48:44.130 --> 00:48:46.130
We have lots of resuscitation opportunities here.

00:48:46.130 --> 00:48:48.150
You could also repair your ship...

00:48:48.150 --> 00:48:51.710
I don't need any repairs!

00:48:51.710 --> 00:48:54.700
And a man can take a vacation after we've invaded your country.

00:48:54.700 --> 00:49:00.000
You could also take Ivanovitsa's virginity personally.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:03.240
- What? - I see.

00:49:03.240 --> 00:49:06.880
We need to keep an eye on them.

00:49:06.880 --> 00:49:08.880
Make your position clear.

00:49:08.880 --> 00:49:10.470
- There is Ansa!

00:49:10.470 --> 00:49:14.920
- They are nothing to us, we'll take them as security guards!

00:49:14.920 --> 00:49:18.610
- And they clearly need a vacation.

00:49:18.610 --> 00:49:22.160
And these ships are a bit small.

00:49:22.160 --> 00:49:23.140
- Of course.

00:49:23.140 --> 00:49:26.900
- Okay, Sherrypie, we accept your offer.

00:49:26.900 --> 00:49:29.890
Paapel 13 is officially part of the P-Union.

00:49:30.030 --> 00:49:30.960
It's called...

00:49:30.960 --> 00:49:36.630
"Pirk's superior position"

00:49:36.630 --> 00:49:41.580
Well if you don't say so, we'll get some new ones!

00:49:41.580 --> 00:49:44.560
"Pirk out"

00:49:44.560 --> 00:49:48.790
"Dwarf, call all the operational security men and gather them all to the shelter"

00:49:48.790 --> 00:49:53.070
"You and Info, stay here at Potkustart"

00:49:53.070 --> 00:49:54.130
"All on your guard"

00:49:54.130 --> 00:49:58.550
"If they try to cheat, shoot the station to shit!"

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:01.990
Especially after I got out of there.

00:50:01.990 --> 00:50:18.430
Emperor Raapustus.

00:50:18.430 --> 00:50:20.570
What time is it?

00:50:20.570 --> 00:50:24.570
P-Union crushed Paapeliin Pellei's laughing ship lightly.

00:50:24.570 --> 00:50:26.710
And now their support is in my hands.

00:50:26.710 --> 00:50:29.530
We take this station under control.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:34.020
and we'll spend some time there before we go and conquer their planet.

00:50:34.020 --> 00:50:37.000
The men can rest a bit and...

00:50:37.000 --> 00:50:47.030
...I think I have something to offer too.

00:50:47.030 --> 00:50:48.090
"Kiikari!"

00:50:48.090 --> 00:50:49.240
"Aaah!"

00:51:01.020 --> 00:51:04.930
Emperor's white suit requires immediate permission to descend.

00:51:04.930 --> 00:51:09.150
Permission granted, Hanna Rykkösen. Welcome to the station.

00:51:09.150 --> 00:51:12.990
Oh my god.

00:51:12.990 --> 00:51:14.940
This seems a bit too easy.

00:51:14.940 --> 00:51:15.940
Indeed.

00:51:15.940 --> 00:51:19.620
Hey kid, I guess you have your conscience in order?

00:51:19.620 --> 00:51:20.790
Yes.

00:51:20.790 --> 00:51:22.790
I know in my heart that we're not going back on this trip.

00:51:22.790 --> 00:51:24.790
What? This can't be such a bad show.

00:51:24.790 --> 00:51:26.740
No, it can't.

00:51:26.740 --> 00:51:30.000
Listen, last time when it had to be an easy show, my friends covered me with a butcher's knife.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:32.050
I told them, and they stayed on the road.

00:51:32.050 --> 00:51:35.670
And that Japanese guy, Kamikaze, he's probably never going to walk again.

00:51:35.670 --> 00:51:36.740
And that muscle was...

00:51:36.740 --> 00:51:37.830
Silence!

00:51:37.830 --> 00:51:39.860
You're counting men's brains!

00:51:39.860 --> 00:51:53.270
Everyone ready?

00:51:53.270 --> 00:51:59.830
And what the hell are you talking about?

00:52:03.800 --> 00:52:06.860
Sherrypie can still pay for this.

00:52:06.860 --> 00:52:08.480
Let's go!

00:52:55.630 --> 00:52:56.630
Where's Serifaya?

00:52:56.630 --> 00:53:00.000
He couldn't bear to lose, so he shot himself in the head.

00:53:00.190 --> 00:53:04.080
Three times. I can show you the room if you want to check.

00:53:04.080 --> 00:53:08.910
No, I don't want to. But you could show this station, because this time it's mine.

00:53:08.910 --> 00:53:11.950
Yes, sir. What would you like to see first?

00:53:11.950 --> 00:53:17.770
Well, if we start with your bedroom, because the sheriff promises everything.

00:53:17.770 --> 00:53:20.940
Yes, sir.

00:53:20.940 --> 00:53:29.830
This is Emperor Pirk. All the members of the family who have a couple's registration number at the beginning can come to the station.

00:53:30.320 --> 00:53:33.010
You can't disturb me for the next quarter...

00:53:33.010 --> 00:53:34.930
...hour.

00:53:34.930 --> 00:53:38.860
Let's go.

00:53:38.860 --> 00:53:46.510
♪ I care about my husband. ♪

00:53:46.510 --> 00:53:48.850
♪ I'm used to saying... ♪

00:53:48.850 --> 00:53:50.930
♪ "I'm waiting for you!" ♪

00:54:51.600 --> 00:54:52.120
If not...

00:55:01.850 --> 00:55:06.690
I don't want to be a woman, no matter how many things I do.

00:55:06.690 --> 00:55:07.650
Emperor.

00:55:07.650 --> 00:55:11.160
Yes!

00:55:20.130 --> 00:55:28.340
The viewers should now be properly calibrated to perceive this dimension.

00:55:28.340 --> 00:55:29.800
Hmm, interesting.

00:55:30.030 --> 00:56:00.000
The geese noticed the energy stream in the back of the jump port in the super space. I'll make some adjustments.

00:56:00.250 --> 00:56:01.430
What the hell is that?

00:56:01.430 --> 00:56:02.380
No idea.

00:56:02.380 --> 00:56:04.050
Just an SD card.

00:56:04.050 --> 00:56:06.120
Sir! Sir!

00:56:06.120 --> 00:56:16.880
Damn it! This is Anssa!

00:56:16.880 --> 00:56:19.820
Good day.

00:56:19.820 --> 00:56:26.600
Excavator's reinforcements have arrived.

00:56:34.160 --> 00:56:44.350
We were just testing the new ship of the earth when we heard a little problem and decided to rescue the helper for a moment.

00:56:44.350 --> 00:56:46.450
Where is Captain Gidiap?

00:56:46.450 --> 00:56:50.700
He is a little weak, so he has to leave the ship to my command.

00:56:50.700 --> 00:56:55.080
I would never have dared to say this, but nice to see your face.

00:56:55.080 --> 00:57:00.000
Let's kick those assholes out of here!

00:57:11.080 --> 00:57:14.240
This is captain Joni K. Sherrypie.

00:57:14.240 --> 00:57:17.310
The rumors about my death are widely spread.

00:57:17.310 --> 00:57:19.220
Oh, fuck.

00:57:19.220 --> 00:57:25.270
From now on, we will take back our positions from these cold-blooded scumbags.

00:57:25.270 --> 00:57:29.700
Men of Babel, hold your weapons.

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:32.600
Defend what's rightfully ours.

00:57:32.600 --> 00:57:35.910
Red sector, march, march to Tsikala!

00:57:35.910 --> 00:57:40.690
I declare all members of the P-league to be held in custody according to Law No. 62 of the Constitution.

00:57:40.690 --> 00:57:43.640
Do not let them escape from the station.

00:57:43.640 --> 00:57:48.710
Our reinforcement team will take care of their fleet.

00:57:48.710 --> 00:57:52.630
To all the members of the P-league who surrender without resistance.

00:57:52.630 --> 00:57:56.650
I promise the rightful transfer of war rights and swift expulsion.

00:58:02.110 --> 00:58:08.040
Behind the station there is a Z-Emilie X-51-4 registered vehicle parked in the parking lot.

00:58:08.040 --> 00:58:10.470
We are asking to move the vehicle as soon as possible.

00:58:30.250 --> 00:58:40.390
Activate the defense network and turn on the fire.

00:58:40.390 --> 00:58:43.100
I'm the one who killed Hansa!

00:58:43.100 --> 00:58:45.250
I'll kill you!

00:58:45.250 --> 00:58:52.950
KILL ME!

00:58:52.950 --> 00:58:55.010
Heelich, you're the spy.

00:58:55.010 --> 00:58:57.730
The Emperor and half of our men are still at the station.

00:58:57.730 --> 00:59:00.000
Then at least we'll destroy their ships!

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:02.800
Disperse to the shipyard! Turn the lights on and prepare for fire!

00:59:02.800 --> 00:59:06.040
I'm sorry, I think the comment was left for me.

00:59:06.040 --> 00:59:09.510
Disperse to the shipyard. Forget the comment just now.

00:59:09.510 --> 00:59:12.910
Turn the lights on to the enemy ships and fire at them.

00:59:12.910 --> 00:59:16.460
The shipyard declares that the lights have run out.

00:59:16.460 --> 00:59:20.920
Hm. In that case, we proceed with full force to the escape distance.

00:59:20.920 --> 00:59:24.780
Our casualties are likely to rise to over 68.4%.

00:59:24.780 --> 00:59:27.010
Maybe today is a reasonable day to die.

00:59:50.960 --> 00:59:54.000
Don't worry, I'll take care of this.

00:59:54.000 --> 00:59:55.950
But don't go, you're human.

00:59:55.950 --> 00:59:57.840
It's my destiny.

01:00:11.320 --> 01:00:16.580
I will kill people in this war.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:36.010
Kaiser Pirk, order your men to drop their weapons immediately, so we can all be given full war rights.

01:00:36.010 --> 01:00:40.840
You guys have never given any!

01:00:40.840 --> 01:00:43.960
What happened? I lost my communicator.

01:00:43.960 --> 01:00:49.730
Ivanovitsa, take contact with the enemy fleet and tell them that we have captured their emperor.

01:00:49.730 --> 01:00:53.590
Impossible, sir. The last hit damaged our communication system.

01:00:53.590 --> 01:00:54.770
Fuck.

01:00:54.770 --> 01:00:59.280
Alright, I have no use for you anymore. Can I go now?

01:01:10.400 --> 01:01:11.360
The army has been defeated!

01:01:11.360 --> 01:01:12.550
The army has been defeated!

01:01:12.550 --> 01:01:27.510
I became free.

01:01:27.510 --> 01:01:28.520
I became free.

01:01:28.520 --> 01:01:29.520
I joined the army.

01:01:29.520 --> 01:01:30.000
I defended the country, all of it.

01:01:30.480 --> 01:01:33.420
against the enemy.

01:01:33.420 --> 01:01:35.420
I have defended a common land,

01:01:35.420 --> 01:01:37.420
against the ferocious barbarians of Mars

01:01:37.420 --> 01:01:40.850
and against the ships of the minibars.

01:01:40.850 --> 01:01:43.990
I have protected all of that

01:01:43.990 --> 01:01:48.450
from a common land.

01:01:48.450 --> 01:01:50.300
FROM A COMMON HUMAN BEING!

01:01:50.300 --> 01:01:52.570
DON'T TALK ABOUT ME!

01:01:52.570 --> 01:01:55.290
What if you're that eager to die?

01:01:55.290 --> 01:02:00.000
Emperor Pirk,

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:07.370
On the grounds of Article 42 of the war law, I condemn you to death for crimes against humanity.

01:02:07.370 --> 01:02:13.160
The execution takes place immediately at the five head-on plasma ballerinas.

01:02:13.160 --> 01:02:15.420
Well, what's wrong with that?!

01:02:15.420 --> 01:02:17.420
Damn, I can't even hold it!

01:02:17.420 --> 01:02:18.790
Valmina!

01:02:18.790 --> 01:02:24.560
Come here!

01:02:24.560 --> 01:02:25.760
Turkanen!

01:02:25.760 --> 01:02:29.960
Wouldn't you be able to support these roof structures properly?

01:03:05.150 --> 01:03:06.880
-

01:04:32.670 --> 01:04:34.900
I'm going somewhere, Emperor.

01:04:34.900 --> 01:04:41.980
What the fuck are these buildings?

01:04:41.980 --> 01:04:43.000
Whoa!

01:04:43.000 --> 01:04:46.750
This station is a piece of shit anyway! Not even a Turbo Hiss!

01:04:47.350 --> 01:04:53.370
Movement only does you good!

01:04:53.370 --> 01:04:54.990
Yeah, movement.

01:04:54.990 --> 01:04:59.320
Don't you have a TV shop? I ordered this from there and it started well.

01:05:06.810 --> 01:05:09.810
Get out of there, get out of there!

01:05:10.950 --> 01:05:13.100
What is this fire again?

01:05:13.100 --> 01:05:18.730
My Fagerholm, I ran out of batteries.

01:05:18.730 --> 01:05:23.210
Let's take care of this properly.

01:05:23.210 --> 01:05:27.490
Man against man.

01:06:00.440 --> 01:06:03.710
Get out of my way!

01:06:10.800 --> 01:06:17.270
Well then, Emperor. The game is over.

01:06:17.270 --> 01:06:21.160
Understand this, Pirk. War is war.

01:06:21.160 --> 01:06:25.530
As soldiers, we both know better than anyone.

01:06:25.530 --> 01:06:28.530
But at the time when you cold-bloodedly killed my friend...

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:39.230
The world turned into a personal place. I'm going to make sure you die slowly. And I'm going to make sure you get rid of your work every single detail.

01:06:39.230 --> 01:06:43.460
You shouldn't keep shoes that long.

01:06:43.460 --> 01:06:49.300
Huh? My penis!

01:06:49.300 --> 01:06:52.670
Found it!

01:06:52.670 --> 01:06:54.670
I'll throw you into the hangar!

01:06:54.670 --> 01:06:56.240
You'll choke!

01:07:20.600 --> 01:07:27.450
Let's move on to the next target.

01:07:27.450 --> 01:07:28.840
Sir, we can hear you.

01:07:30.860 --> 01:07:33.780
I'm here for you, come and get me as soon as possible!

01:07:33.780 --> 01:07:36.130
Those fucking rogues had organized a raid on me!

01:07:36.130 --> 01:07:37.630
That's true, sir.

01:07:37.630 --> 01:07:39.630
But they didn't do anything to my safety!

01:07:46.610 --> 01:07:48.170
Course towards the emperor's base.

01:07:48.170 --> 01:07:50.650
Wait! Let's deal with this one destroyer first.

01:07:50.650 --> 01:07:53.470
Commander, this is an imperial emergency call.

01:07:53.470 --> 01:07:54.970
Let's leave immediately.

01:07:54.970 --> 01:07:57.380
You were just about to. This will be dealt with in a moment.

01:07:57.380 --> 01:08:00.000
I don't know what you have in use on the planet of apes.

01:08:00.280 --> 01:08:02.480
but in the P-Union they take a higher up-series.

01:08:02.480 --> 01:08:04.800
And now you're enough to disturb my magnetic brain!

01:08:04.800 --> 01:08:14.300
What do you mean, LOSDA?

01:08:32.240 --> 01:08:36.930
As you might have thought, the video's remote stop button doesn't work.

01:08:36.930 --> 01:09:00.000
And now hopefully we can go to help the emperor.

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:02.000
Go on a little holiday.

01:09:02.000 --> 01:09:04.590
Oh, damn it!

01:09:04.590 --> 01:09:06.410
Go around the enemy's side.

01:09:06.410 --> 01:09:09.440
I want the heavy fighters out of the game right now!

01:09:35.050 --> 01:09:42.390
"Rate is clear, sir!"

01:10:16.480 --> 01:10:19.580
Where are you guys, by the way?

01:10:19.580 --> 01:10:20.530
Fuck off!

01:10:20.530 --> 01:10:22.090
We came as close as we could.

01:10:22.090 --> 01:10:24.980
In the limits of Commander Dwarf's operational capabilities.

01:10:24.980 --> 01:10:27.550
War cannot be won by avoiding battles.

01:10:27.550 --> 01:10:30.000
Enough with that awful bling-on slander.

01:10:31.400 --> 01:10:32.660
Situation report.

01:10:32.660 --> 01:10:38.350
We have lost 23 units, there are still 14 operational units.

01:10:38.350 --> 01:10:41.350
The enemy reinforcements are making a sharp counter attack.

01:10:41.350 --> 01:10:45.350
In addition, the solar radiation doesn't get through the main line's more advanced armor.

01:10:45.350 --> 01:10:46.450
What the fuck?

01:10:46.450 --> 01:10:49.430
Are these our flashlights, or what?

01:10:49.430 --> 01:10:55.630
The light bulbs seem to be more powerful, but there are only nine left on the kickstart.

01:10:55.630 --> 01:10:57.760
Let's put them all at once, isn't that right?

01:10:57.760 --> 01:11:00.000
And 12, this is an important box.

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:01.900
So I'll take control of the gun.

01:11:01.900 --> 01:11:04.880
Sir, I don't recommend it.

01:11:04.880 --> 01:11:09.300
Maybe this distance is a bit too much for you, but for me this isn't a trick or anything.

01:11:09.300 --> 01:11:12.520
Computer, hand-guided control of the gun system.

01:11:14.080 --> 01:11:17.960
This is child's play.

01:11:50.640 --> 01:11:57.010
Oh, fuck. - You asshole.

01:12:00.760 --> 01:12:02.760
But it was on target!

01:12:02.760 --> 01:12:06.330
You saw it, didn't you?

01:12:06.330 --> 01:12:08.330
Sir, have you ever heard of prediction?

01:12:08.330 --> 01:12:10.250
Prediction?

01:12:10.250 --> 01:12:14.370
Don't these fucking computers know how to predict from my side?

01:12:14.370 --> 01:12:17.250
When you're on target, then you have to hit it!

01:12:21.500 --> 01:12:23.500
Kid's toy, indeed.

01:12:23.500 --> 01:12:25.440
Well, you haven't hit it, you fucking...

01:12:25.440 --> 01:12:29.300
How did you hear that sound?

01:12:33.290 --> 01:12:39.280
Sir, the attack just now would have caused heavy casualties.

01:12:39.280 --> 01:12:43.320
The enemy command unit may be a great threat to us.

01:12:43.320 --> 01:12:49.070
Well, an attack is the best defense. Do something about it.

01:12:49.070 --> 01:12:53.940
Check the target and prepare the main gun.

01:13:00.570 --> 01:13:02.570
I'm going to destroy Styrbur's heavy armor!

01:13:02.570 --> 01:13:04.660
Oh yeah, shoot now!

01:13:04.660 --> 01:13:07.210
The enemy cruiser is targeting us with its main gun.

01:13:07.210 --> 01:13:09.610
Well, do your regional operations then!

01:13:09.610 --> 01:13:11.810
Regional operations, Pirp 7.

01:13:36.940 --> 01:13:40.920
You have 40 seconds to return to normal.

01:13:40.920 --> 01:13:53.210
It would be nice to get to see what the commander-in-chief of this ship has planned.

01:13:53.210 --> 01:13:59.160
According to my estimate, the enemy commander can fire again in 7.3 seconds.

01:14:03.520 --> 01:14:06.340
Now I figured it out. Let's hide behind the station.

01:14:06.340 --> 01:14:29.060
At least they won't dare to shoot there.

01:14:31.560 --> 01:14:33.840
And where is our friend Potkustart?

01:14:33.840 --> 01:14:35.490
I don't know, sir.

01:14:35.490 --> 01:14:39.780
The computer was missing in connection with the power outage, so we lost the recording.

01:14:39.780 --> 01:14:46.810
But we'll have to stop it right there. Just a moment.

01:14:46.810 --> 01:14:50.580
Captain Raapustus.

01:14:50.580 --> 01:14:57.320
We suffered heavy blows to the control circles of the hammerhead, and we had to perform repairs.

01:14:57.320 --> 01:15:00.000
Most of the crew was at the beginning of the battle.

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:03.000
and now the door is closed.

01:15:03.000 --> 01:15:07.210
Lieutenant Makarov, how are the repairs going?

01:15:07.210 --> 01:15:10.980
Can't we get the door open within 10 minutes, sir?

01:15:10.980 --> 01:15:15.250
No rush. The fight continues.

01:15:31.050 --> 01:15:33.980
Damn it!

01:15:33.980 --> 01:15:36.090
Ouch!

01:15:36.090 --> 01:15:38.090
Oh, damn it!

01:15:38.090 --> 01:15:40.500
Guys, no!

01:15:40.500 --> 01:15:43.500
According to the scouts, there are still 20 light balls left in Kalinka.

01:15:43.500 --> 01:15:46.900
What the hell has gone wrong again?

01:15:46.900 --> 01:15:48.820
Calm down, sir.

01:15:48.820 --> 01:15:53.820
If we only ask Captain Fakovia to operate the light balls for the kickstart, we can get close enough.

01:15:53.820 --> 01:15:57.210
And shoot it to pieces!

01:15:57.210 --> 01:15:59.210
Although I could manage the aiming this time.

01:15:59.210 --> 01:15:59.800
No!

01:16:00.860 --> 01:16:02.590
I'll take care of it.

01:16:02.590 --> 01:16:06.760
The Emperor of Honor is about to break his neck.

01:16:06.760 --> 01:16:09.440
Shoot me then, but...

01:16:09.440 --> 01:16:11.040
...be sure to hit me!

01:16:11.040 --> 01:16:16.200
I'm in touch with Fagov!

01:16:16.200 --> 01:16:21.930
*cough*

01:16:21.930 --> 01:16:23.160
Hello!

01:16:23.160 --> 01:16:25.050
What have you gone to do?!

01:16:25.050 --> 01:16:26.960
I haven't hit you once and...

01:16:26.960 --> 01:16:28.450
...the ship's a piece of shit!

01:16:28.450 --> 01:16:29.120
*cough*

01:16:32.910 --> 01:16:34.690
...technical problems.

01:16:34.690 --> 01:16:37.560
Now you are going to put the Kalinka here...

01:16:37.560 --> 01:16:41.970
...and you are going to put all the light bulbs you have on the shelf.

01:16:41.970 --> 01:16:48.660
And you are going to bring them to the kickstart.

01:16:48.660 --> 01:16:50.260
What?!

01:16:50.260 --> 01:16:52.880
This connection is breaking!

01:16:52.880 --> 01:16:56.210
Just send the whole battery here.

01:16:56.210 --> 01:16:57.440
Yeah...

01:16:57.440 --> 01:17:00.000
Pack them properly, so they don't get stuck in the ground.

01:17:08.090 --> 01:17:20.310
Okay.

01:17:20.310 --> 01:17:25.900
Sir, the enemy fleet is forcing our ships to attack.

01:17:25.900 --> 01:17:29.140
Should we retreat and regroup?

01:17:29.140 --> 01:17:29.730
No.

01:17:36.240 --> 01:17:38.240
If you have located the kickstart.

01:17:38.240 --> 01:17:40.980
Yes, sir. It's very close to Babel 13.

01:17:40.980 --> 01:17:41.940
But our ship...

01:17:41.940 --> 01:17:43.940
They can take care of themselves.

01:17:43.940 --> 01:17:45.620
We will destroy the kickstart.

01:17:45.620 --> 01:17:51.760
I've heard that these backless Nileans are fighting only because they fear the Emperor.

01:17:51.760 --> 01:17:56.600
The failure of the ship crushes the enemy's will to fight and ensures our victory.

01:18:09.880 --> 01:18:13.520
Sir, the charger master of the lightbulb pipe is calling you.

01:18:13.520 --> 01:18:16.510
Emperor, I got a letter from King Kalinka.

01:18:16.510 --> 01:18:18.550
Well, it's been a while.

01:18:18.550 --> 01:18:19.990
What should we do with these?

01:18:19.990 --> 01:18:21.680
What do you think I'm a fool?

01:18:21.680 --> 01:18:24.880
Bring them to the lightbulb pipe!

01:18:24.880 --> 01:18:26.320
Hey, lightbulb charger!

01:18:26.320 --> 01:18:28.680
What am I supposed to do with these lightbulbs?

01:18:28.680 --> 01:18:30.000
I think I'll put them under the table.

01:18:30.030 --> 01:18:31.580
Pino, yeah!

01:18:31.580 --> 01:18:34.230
I'll never get a job in Russia.

01:18:34.230 --> 01:18:37.840
Everything is ready for our plan.

01:18:37.840 --> 01:18:40.080
Show me the cameras.

01:18:40.690 --> 01:18:52.530
Sir!

01:18:52.530 --> 01:18:55.190
The kickstart is about to take off from Babel 13's cover.

01:18:55.190 --> 01:18:57.430
And it's coming straight at us!

01:19:03.900 --> 01:19:08.490
Emperor Pirk here. Is there something to say before we tear you to pieces?

01:19:08.490 --> 01:19:11.630
Ah, Emperor. We finally meet again.

01:19:11.630 --> 01:19:16.800
I'm sorry to disappoint you, but your attack makes me feel almost sorry.

01:19:16.800 --> 01:19:22.150
...after 20 light balls.

01:19:22.150 --> 01:19:30.000
Ready to turn around.

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:36.530
I'll make this a little too easy, but on the other hand, you don't have to look at it in the eye.

01:19:36.530 --> 01:19:38.530
Captain, if you have a request...

01:19:38.530 --> 01:19:43.300
Prepare the main gun.

01:19:43.300 --> 01:19:54.520
Destruction phase, now.

01:19:54.520 --> 01:20:00.000
The Pirck's doorbell rings again.

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:01.820
We're going to the commando bridge!

01:20:01.820 --> 01:20:02.820
Sayonara desolation!

01:20:02.820 --> 01:20:03.900
Fire!

01:20:03.900 --> 01:20:19.240
Mother is a big mother!

01:20:19.240 --> 01:20:21.240
We're going to the commando bridge!

01:20:21.240 --> 01:20:24.930
Using 33 centiliters of beer cans filled with light bulbs.

01:20:30.350 --> 01:20:37.230
-What? -What the hell?

01:20:37.620 --> 01:20:43.380
These light bulbs were mine!

01:20:44.730 --> 01:20:47.720
Light bulbs? What light bulbs?

01:20:48.040 --> 01:20:51.730
I ordered you to send all the light bulbs here.

01:20:51.980 --> 01:20:55.520
You fucking dead fucking mutant!

01:20:55.620 --> 01:20:58.390
No way! You asked for the beer bottles.

01:21:01.880 --> 01:21:03.450
The enemy is approaching the fire!

01:21:03.450 --> 01:21:05.540
- Get out of the way! - Too late.

01:21:05.540 --> 01:21:16.370
- This is an emergency! - The second rotation motor was destroyed!

01:21:16.370 --> 01:21:20.910
- The power banks 3-11 are leaking! - The micro-supply service went bankrupt!

01:21:20.910 --> 01:21:25.960
- The power plant is out of line! - The coffee machine was destroyed to recover!

01:21:43.240 --> 01:21:45.130
It's a tiny machine gun, can you see?

01:21:45.130 --> 01:21:46.950
This bullet has just been dropped.

01:21:46.950 --> 01:21:50.840
It has a refraction heart and anti-material increase all the way.

01:21:50.840 --> 01:21:53.120
Well, fix it!

01:21:53.120 --> 01:21:54.120
Let's shoot!

01:21:54.120 --> 01:21:56.120
Sir, the weapons systems don't work.

01:21:56.120 --> 01:22:00.000
In addition, the kickstart's refraction heart breaks down in 3.6 minutes.

01:22:00.060 --> 01:22:08.100
Well, that bastard is going to join us.

01:22:08.100 --> 01:22:16.590
A crash course.

01:22:16.590 --> 01:22:18.670
A miserable last attempt.

01:22:18.670 --> 01:22:21.160
The next launch will take care of them.

01:22:21.160 --> 01:22:22.220
Captain!

01:22:22.220 --> 01:22:29.300
Prepare your headgear.

01:22:29.300 --> 01:22:29.830
Sir!

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:35.540
I don't know how this is possible, but Kalja seems to have eaten all the control circles.

01:22:35.540 --> 01:22:37.770
The main gun is useless.

01:22:37.770 --> 01:22:43.660
Well, good. Let's do this in a more difficult way.

01:22:43.660 --> 01:22:45.940
Secondary guns, fire!

01:22:57.910 --> 01:23:00.000
You have been a foot-resistant, but these...

01:23:00.000 --> 01:23:02.000
You yourself say that you are already injured.

